# The OpenStreetMap blocks are generated binary, ~32 MB in total and rewritten wholesale by
# `npm run osm`. In plain git every regeneration would add another 32 MB to the history for ever;
# in LFS the history holds pointers and only the current objects are fetched.
#
# Two things have to be true for the deployed site to work: `git lfs install` on any machine that
# commits them, and `lfs: true` on the checkout step in .github/workflows/pages.yml. Without the
# second, the build publishes 130-byte pointer files and every block silently reads as empty.
src/web/public/osm/*.bin filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
